    {
      "id": "dba89ded5127113835ddaa28c24e04a5aa3288bb",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1390817060,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Hi, the capture in #19073 has the SSPI token as SPNEGO ASN.1 BER handled by the spnego dissector. The MS-TDS document spec suggests that the token should be in that form, not sent to GSS-API (unlike the SSPI packet type) when not directly NTLM as in your capture here.\n\nDo you have any examples that ought to call gssapi?",
